I am an extensive user of IPBT, and I recommend r7471 wholeheartedly.

From a development standpoint working on Spork, I make great use of 
the 'search' functionality, primarily while reviewing other
people's ttyrecs after they've reported a bug, or just to see whether
certain things are happening, and how often they happen, etc.

The ability to look for a particular message (such as "A mysterious
force surrounds you") allows me to actually _use_ ttyrecs as a tool,
rather than as just a TV channel.  It reduces the need to ask questions
like "what were you doing at the time _X_ occurred?", since of course I
can just go to that spot, hit 500b to move back a bit, and tap 'p' to
play forward from there.

